{"body":"Accept verified partial findings for 30004435 / OWR-17474-009. The original probability-only proof request remains **unsolved, 5/5**.\n\nSteif's Question C asks for a proof, without entropy, of equality of the completed past and future tails for every stationary finite-alphabet process. The identity is already known by entropy arguments. Those arguments do not resolve the requested method, and the packet does not claim a proof for arbitrary processes.\n\nThe packet gives probability-only finite Markov and finite hidden Markov classifications, including separately proved bilateral classifications and an observable-law quotient with a finite word-span certificate. It proves a full-future coupling bound and equal trivial one-sided tails under uniform overlap and summable all-history continuity, assuming a stationary compatible law exists; its displayed infinite-memory example supplies existence separately. It establishes corresponding tail inclusions for locally decisive codes of finite mean radius, and equality transfer when an inverse code supplies the reverse inclusions. For measurable mixtures of conditionally common-D-stationary alpha-mixing laws it identifies both one-sided tails with the observable conditional-law field, with an additional hypothesis for bilateral equality. Exact weak-limit, heavy-radius, redundant-parameter and irrational-rotation examples expose the limits of these routes. None removes the subclass assumptions from the original target.\n\nAcceptance follows root source-first reconstruction of all five quantified arguments, three independent reviews across distinct mechanisms, a fresh independent whole-package adversarial review, and root reproduction of all complete original outputs plus the new independent mathematical controls. All 210,974 author assertions and 9,334 historical review assertions replay exactly; finite computations supplement the universal written proofs. Four primary PDFs were freshly fetched, read and checked independently. Every original path, historical manifest and author checkpoint binding checks out. No novelty or exhaustive current-openness certification is claimed.\n\nOriginal head: 4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46. Author checkpoint: f1c1e710597b4d9d0993290091f601d086666126. Current queue-only refreshed head: 07f83847edc7b91201c3a71fa8ca694b5172bd6d, with parents [4e635c77d7399d671ea58700e41bbd92cbdeeb46, ef789480d00794adeb841310218b2979bac57caa] and complete tree 1278c533cb2e68aec138db0ef328162025edf7eb. All 52 original mathematical/review/publication files remain byte-identical. Against its current-main parent only this problem's queue status and turn count change on line409; every other path and queue byte is preserved. Historical pending-review statements remain frozen history, with the accepted disposition recorded in the descending audit. Final exact current-state verification and actual merge are required before acceptance is complete.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in deriving, checking and reviewing these findings. This is independent AI-assisted verification, not external human peer review or formal proof-assistant certification. Prior results, theorem dependencies, subclass assumptions and the unrestricted gap are explicit. Merge only as a partial result: no preprint, Zenodo upload, DOI, tracker row or release is produced for this unsolved problem.\n\nAudit artifacts: draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr373_30004435 on main.\n","headRefOid":"07f83847edc7b91201c3a71fa8ca694b5172bd6d","isDraft":false,"mergeCommit":null,"mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","mergedAt":null,"state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/373"}
